2026-09-27T09:10:28.1712278Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1712649Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1713166Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1713645Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1713803Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1714174Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1714406Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1714688Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1715758Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1716179Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1716460Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1717318Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1717682Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1718110Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1719061Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1719949Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1721371Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1722565Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1723338Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1724289Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1725770Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1726412Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1727150Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1727885Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1728036Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1728376Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1728733Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1805495Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1808420Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1808790Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1809377Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1810369Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1811036Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1811643Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1812133Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1812580Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1812707Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1812996Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1813171Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1814232Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1815623Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1816309Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1817219Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:28.1817458Z 
